# MatchVaga Project Overview

## Product

**MatchVaga** is a SaaS platform that:
1. **Analyzes the gap** between a user's resume and a job description
2. **Identifies missing skills** required for the target role
3. **Generates an optimized document** (PDF/DOCX) tailored to the job

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technology |
|-------|------------|
| Framework | Next.js 16 (App Router) |
| React | React 19 |
| Auth | Supabase Auth (email OTP, Google OAuth) |
| Backend | Server Actions, Supabase (Postgres + Storage) |
| AI/LLM | Gemini 1.5 Flash (extraction), GPT-4o-mini (scoring, chat), Claude 3.5 Sonnet (synthesis) |
| Validation | Zod |
| Data fetching (client) | TanStack Query v5 |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS v4 |
| UI Components | shadcn/ui (radix-vega style), Base UI, Radix UI |
| Icons | lucide-react |
| Utils | clsx, tailwind-merge, class-variance-authority |

## Project Structure

```
src/
├── app/           # App Router pages, layouts, route groups; route-specific in _components/, _utils/, _hooks/, _constants/, _contexts/, _actions/
│   └── actions/   # Shared Server Actions (resume, job, analysis, document, chat)
├── components/    # ui/ (shadcn primitives) + shared/ (cross-feature components)
├── constants/     # Shared constants (auth, design-tokens, routes, etc.)
├── contexts/      # React Context providers
├── hooks/         # Shared custom hooks (logic layer)
├── lib/           # Supabase client (client.ts, server.ts) + AI utilities (server-only) + query/ (get-query-client, query-options)
├── schemas/       # Zod schemas for Server Action validation
├── utils/         # Shared utilities (style, auth, etc.)
└── types/         # Shared TypeScript interfaces
```

**Component colocation:** See `colocation.mdc`.

**Utils, constants, hooks:** See `colocation.mdc` for placement. See `check-before-add.mdc` before adding new ones.

## Route Architecture

| Route Group | Layout | Purpose |
|-------------|--------|---------|
| `(auth)/` | Full-screen, brand primary override | Login (email → token flow) |
| `(legal)/` | Minimal `bg-background` wrapper | Privacy policy, Terms of service |
| `onboarding/` | Top bar + step indicator | Resume upload → verify flow |
| `dashboard/` | *(TBD — sidebar layout)* | Main app after onboarding |

Route groups `(auth)` and `(legal)` use parenthesized folders to share layouts without affecting the URL.

## Path Aliases

- `@/components` — Components (ui/, shared/)
- `@/constants` — Shared constants (auth, design-tokens, routes, etc.)
- `@/components/ui` — shadcn UI primitives
- `@/lib/supabase` — Supabase client (client, server)
- `@/lib/ai` — AI prompts and client wrappers (server-only)
- `@/lib/query` — Query client, query options
- `@/components/shared` — Cross-feature components (e.g. brand)
- `@/contexts` — Context providers
- `@/hooks` — Custom hooks
- `@/utils/style` — cn() helper (clsx + tailwind-merge)
- `@/utils/auth` — Auth utilities (translateAuthError for Supabase errors)
- `@/types` — Shared type definitions

Route-local utils/hooks/constants use relative imports (e.g. `./_utils/...`, `../_hooks/...`). See `colocation.mdc`.

