## Keeping Rules Updated

When the project changes, update these rules accordingly:

| Change | Update |
|--------|--------|
| New important library | Add to Tech Stack table |
| New folder in `src/` | Add to Project Structure; update path aliases if new |
| New path alias | Add to Path Aliases; update `components.json` reference |
| New util function | Add to `utils/<domain>.ts` (shared) or `_utils/` (route-specific); see `colocation.mdc` |
| New shared constant (2+ routes) | Add to `constants/<domain>.ts`; route-specific → `_constants/`; single constant → keep in component/module |
| New query options/keys/hooks | Add to `lib/query/`, `constants/query-keys.ts`, or `hooks/` per colocation; update this rule |
| New route group or flow | Add to Route Architecture |
| New domain concept | Add to `matchvaga-domain.mdc` |
| New AI flow or provider | Add to `matchvaga-domain.mdc`; document env vars in `security.mdc` |
| New design components or tokens | Update `design-tokens-reference.mdc`, `design-components.mdc`, and `globals.css` / `design-tokens.ts` |
| New security surface | Update `security.mdc` |
| New Server Action | Add to `app/actions/` or route `_actions/`; validate with Zod |
| New DB table or migration | Update `database-schema.mdc` |
| App Router patterns, loading/error, use cache | See `nextjs-app-router.mdc` |
| React purity, hooks, Thinking in React | See `react-rules.mdc` |
| Editing rules | See `rule-writing-guidelines.mdc` |
| New MCP server | Update `mcp-tools.mdc` and `.cursor/mcp.json` |
| Linear task template change | Update `linear-task-template.mdc` |
